>> title: Chili Powder
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: tex-mex, chiles, spice blend, toasted, pantry
>> servings: 16
>> time: 25 min
>> step.1: toast in a dry skillet 2 min
>> step.2: add, toast 1 min more
>> step.3: cool, grind fine
>> step.4: whisk in

Toast @dried ancho chiles{4}(stemmed, seeded, torn up), @dried guajillo chiles{3}(stemmed, seeded, torn up), and @dried chiles de arbol{2}(stemmed) in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat until they smell like raisins, about ~{2%min}.

Add @cumin seeds{1%Tbs} to @&(~1)toasted chiles{} and toast ~{1%min} more, then stir in @dried Mexican oregano{1%Tbs} off the heat.

Cool @&(~1)mixture{} completely, then grind to a fine powder in a #spice grinder{}.

Whisk @garlic powder{1%Tbs}, @onion powder{1%Tbs}, and @smoked paprika{1%tsp} into @&(~1)powder{}.
